SUMMARY:Deadline: Nederlands Letterenfonds: Project Grants for Literary Tra
 nslators (August 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Project subsidies from the Nederlands Letterenfonds for advance
 d literary translators with a current publishing contract for a translatio
 n from or into Dutch. The next round closes 15 August 2026\; decisions are
  made approximately four months after the deadline (December). ELIGIBILITY
 : literary translators with a substantial published portfolio and a contra
 cted translation project\; primary income must be below EUR 52\,500.\n\nOr
 ganisation: Nederlands Letterenfonds (Dutch Foundation for Literature)\nLo
 cation: Worldwide (literary translators with a contracted translation from
  or into Dutch)\nAward: Project-based subsidy. Income cap EUR 52\,500 for 
 primary income. Standard minimum rates: EUR 0.0802/word for prose\; EUR 2.
 92/line for poetry. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\, scaled 
 to the contracted translation\n\nMore: https://www.letterenfonds.nl/en-car
 ibbean/funding/project-grants-for-literary-translators?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.letterenfonds.nl/en-caribbean/funding/project-grants-for-li
 terary-translators?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
LOCATION:Worldwide (literary translators with a contracted translation from
  or into Dutch)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:twente-postdoc-llms4eu-ethics-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261006T142902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260825
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:Deadline: University of Twente: Postdoc\, Ethics and Epistemology o
 f LLMs4EU (17 months)
DESCRIPTION:A postdoctoral position in the Philosophy section at the Univer
 sity of Twente\, part of the 4TU.Center for Ethics and Technology\, workin
 g on the ethics and epistemology strand (Work Package 6) of LLMs4EU. LLMs4
 EU is a European Commission funded initiative led by the Alliance for Lang
 uage Technologies\, spanning more than 20 countries\, to build large langu
 age models across all EU languages and preserve European linguistic and cu
 ltural diversity in the digital age while keeping the resulting tools comp
 liant with European values and legislation including the AI Act and the GD
 PR. TASKS: establish benchmarking frameworks that address legal and ethica
 l concerns\; develop guidelines for fine-tuning processes with an emphasis
  on preserving cultural heritage\; oversee ethics compliance and advise th
 e project ethics board\; and build frameworks that integrate ethical consi
 derations into LLM design. This is the tech-communication and language-pol
 itics end of AI research rather than a modelling job: the questions are wh
 ose language\, whose culture and whose norms get encoded when a continent 
 builds its own models. REQUIREMENTS: a doctorate in ethics\, philosophy\, 
 science and technology studies\, AI ethics\, computer science with an ethi
 cs focus\, or a related field\; demonstrated expertise in AI ethics and et
 hics compliance\; understanding of AI tool design and LLM development\; ap
 preciation for cultural diversity\; strong communication and organisationa
 l skills\; and professional English. Apply through the AcademicTransfer po
 sting. Closes 25 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: University of Twente\, Phil
 osophy section / 4TU.Center for Ethics and Technology\nLocation: Enschede\
 , Netherlands\nAward: EUR 4\,241 to 5\,538 gross per month (scale 10\, ste
 ps 4 to 12) at 1.0 FTE\, plus 8 percent holiday allowance and an 8.3 perce
 nt year-end bonus.\nDuration: 17 months\, full-time (38 to 40 hours per we
 ek)\, with possible extension\n\nMore: https://www.academictransfer.com/en
 /jobs/362444/postdoctoral-researcher-17-months-ethics-and-epistemology-of-
 llms4eu-design-data-and-deployment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/362444/postdoctoral-researcher
 -17-months-ethics-and-epistemology-of-llms4eu-design-data-and-deployment/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Enschede\, Netherlands
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondsbjp-dossiersubsidie-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261006T142902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fonds BJP: Dossiersubsidie for Freelance Regional and Loc
 al Journalists (autumn 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:The Dossiersubsidie is the Fonds BJP scheme for freelance regio
 nal and local journalists in the Netherlands who want to follow one subjec
 t properly rather than chase daily news\, funding up to EUR 19\,200 for si
 x months of sustained reporting on a single dossier. It is aimed at the ga
 p left by shrinking regional newsrooms\, where structural coverage of loca
 l government\, housing\, care or industry rarely gets paid time. ELIGIBILI
 TY: freelance journalists working in Dutch regional and local media only (
 staff journalists and national-only reporters are directed to the fund's o
 ther schemes). The fund also runs a year-round Vooronderzoekssubsidie of u
 p to EUR 8\,800 for preliminary research and a year-round Uitvoeringssubsi
 die of up to EUR 38\,600 for carrying out projects\, both open to all jour
 nalists. APPLICATION WINDOW: 17 August to 14 September 2026\, via the Fond
 s BJP subsidy portal. Online office hours on 8 September 2026\; questions 
 on 020 63 86 295.\n\nOrganisation: Fonds Bijzondere Journalistieke Project
 en (Fonds BJP)\nLocation: Netherlands\; for freelance journalists working 
 on Dutch regional and local reporting\nAward: Up to EUR 19\,200 for six mo
 nths of work on a single reporting dossier. No application fee.\nDuration:
  Six months of dedicated reporting on one subject area\n\nMore: https://ww
 w.fondsbjp.nl/subsidies/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://www.fondsbjp.nl/subsidies/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands\; for freelance journalists working on Dutch regional 
 and local reporting
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rhizome-hartwig-amsterdam-city-fellow-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261006T142902Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261012
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:Deadline: Rhizome x Hartwig Art Foundation: Amsterdam City Fellow (
 two-year digital art research fellowship)
DESCRIPTION:Rhizome and Hartwig Art Foundation are appointing a part-time A
 msterdam City Fellow to build community connections and strengthen engagem
 ent with digital art and creative technology practices in the region. The 
 City Fellowship is a new Rhizome initiative that embeds researchers and wr
 iters in institutions and cities around the world\; the inaugural edition 
 started in July 2026 in Bangalore. THE WORK: research and connect with dig
 ital art communities and practitioners in Amsterdam\, participate in ongoi
 ng collaborative research\, write a monthly newsletter\, conduct interview
 s\, and more. The fellow should also plan to attend Extreme Presence\, a g
 athering on technology\, consciousness and devotion in Amsterdam\, 23 to 2
 5 October 2026 (tickets provided). PARTNER: Hartwig Art Foundation fosters
  the production\, presentation\, communication and preservation of contemp
 orary art and is currently developing the Hartwig Museum\, a major new con
 temporary art museum in Amsterdam scheduled to open in 2028. TERMS: fellow
 s must be based in Amsterdam\; EUR 1\,200 per month stipend at roughly 2 d
 ays per week\, working remotely with optional use of the foundation's offi
 ces. DEADLINE: 12 October 2026\, 12:00 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: Rhizome\, in
  partnership with Hartwig Art Foundation\nLocation: Amsterdam\, Netherland
 s. Fellows must be based in Amsterdam\; work is remote on your own compute
 r\, with the option to work from the Hartwig Art Foundation offices as nee
 ded.\nAward: EUR 1\,200 per month stipend for a part-time commitment of ro
 ughly 2 days per week\, over a two-year term (about EUR 28\,800 total). Ti
 ckets to the Extreme Presence gathering provided. No application fee indic
 ated.\nDuration: Two years\, part-time (about 2 days per week).\n\nMore: h
 ttps://rhizome.org/editorial/2026/oct/01/apply-to-be-an-amsterdam-city-fel
 low/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://rhizome.org/editorial/2026/oct/01/apply-to-be-an-amsterdam-city
 -fellow/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Amsterdam\, Netherlands. Fellows must be based in Amsterdam\; work
  is remote on your own computer\, with the option to work from the Hartwig
  Art Foundation offices as needed.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
